@startuml overview
title Start here: one file of customer records in, one ID per person or company out
left to right direction
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F4F6F8
  BorderColor #65717E
}
skinparam file {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E6
  BorderColor #B07D00
}

file "<b>Customer records</b>\nParquet, columns of any name" as input
rectangle "<b>Load</b>\nread and check the file;\nwrite each fact one way;\nperson or company" as load
rectangle "<b>Rules</b>\nthe certain cases:\nthe same ID and name,\nname, address and phone" as rules
rectangle "<b>The model</b>\nlist the pairs worth scoring;\nscore each in bits of evidence,\nlearned from the file itself" as model
rectangle "<b>Cluster</b>\naccept the sure pairs;\njoin pairs into entities" as cluster
file "<b>gold.parquet</b>\neach record's entity\nand its kind" as gold
file "<b>review sheets</b>\npairs just below the line;\nrecords person or company\nisn't sure of" as sheets
actor "people" as people
file "<b>config/final.toml</b>\nchosen once, on synthetic records\nwhose truth is known;\n<b>config/kind_names.npz</b>, the name model" as config

input --> load
load --> rules
rules --> model
model --> cluster
cluster --> gold
cluster --> sheets
sheets --> people
people --> cluster : decisions
people --> load : answers
config ..> load : the rules, keys, model and threshold

legend right
  The run's nine steps, each with its code, its cost and the tables it
  makes and uses: docs/architecture.md, section 4 (LLD 1)
endlegend
@enduml
